.env
.youtube_token.json
output/
# music/ is committed now: it is 1.5 MB of background tracks, and a cloud
# runner that cannot find them publishes silent videos without saying so.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.venv-tts/
venv/
env/
history.json
agent.log

# Throwaway comparison artefacts from tuning voices, visuals and motion.
voice_samples/
compare/
story_test/

# Anything that could carry a credential. The YouTube token grants upload
# access to the channel, so a stray copy is as dangerous as the original.
*.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*token*.json
*credential*.json
*secret*
client_secret*.json
*.pem
*.key

# 3D assets used to be ignored on the reasoning that code is committed and
# binaries are not, since Mixamo and three.js can supply them again. That held
# while the only machine rendering was this one. A scheduled cloud runner has
# no Downloads folder to fetch them from, and a character library nobody can
# reproduce exactly -- these particular Mixamo downloads, at these names -- is
# not really reproducible anyway. ~68 MB, which a private repo carries fine.
scene3d/node_modules/
scene3d/*.mp4
scene3d/job.json

# Scratch jobs and preview stills from tuning the scene.
scene3d/job_*.json
scene3d/peek_*.png
scene3d/v_*.png
scene3d/m_*.png
scene3d/s_*.png
scene3d/row_*.png
scene3d/*.mp4
